   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to renaming the 149th Street Grand Concourse subway station\nthe \"149th Street-Hostos station\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S8294",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8294-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8294\n\nSPONSOR: SERRANO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to renaming the 149th Street Grand Concourse subway\nstation the \"149th Street-Hostos station\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill will rename the 149th Street-Grand Concourse station to the\n\"149th Street-Hostos\" station. The renaming will recognize the impor-\ntance and value of Hostos Community College to the South Bronx community\nby implementing MTA sign changes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. The 149th Street-Grand Concourse subway station is hereby\nrenamed the 149th Street Hostos station. The MTA shall ensure that all\nsigns, maps, and any other items issued by the MTA are updated to accu-\nrately reflect the new name of the stations with a time and in a manner\ndeemed appropriate by the MTA.\n\nSection 2. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nHostos Community College was founded in 1968 to serve the unique educa-\ntional needs of the South Bronx community. Named after Eugenio Maria de\nHostos, the college the college is a beacon for those who have histor-\nically been excluded from the opportunity to go to college, especially\nthose Americans of Dominican and Puerto Rican descent. Hostos Community\nCollege has celebrated Dominican and Puerto Rican culture over the past\n50-plus years. This renaming will further the sense of cultural identity\nand belonging of people in the South Bronx community.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
